{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1423638357,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"59074fc546827fd4586d32f387a2c4a3","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;noo, so I had made a suuper long entry and it got deleted :(. I&#039;ll do my best to replicate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Ok so now the fun begins!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The wedding band&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;this was literally the first thing I bought. I spent more than I had hoped on it, but then I thought that if I was going to spend my money on something, this should be it. I&#039;ll be wearing it for the rest of my life! The band is a matching set with my e-ring, which actually took a lot of work to match. Long story short, it didn&#039;t fit well wit my e-ring so I had to send it back a couple of times until it finally got fixed. It was frustrating to say the least but now I can&#039;t wait to wear it :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\" alt=\"weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Flowers&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;If there is one topic that gets me roiled up, is the price of the natural flowers at the Karisma properties. HOLY COW! that&#039;s all I have to say haha. To give you an idea, they cost more than what I would pay here in Canada, and they don&#039;t allow outside florists. So, I&#039;m boycotting the whole thing and using fake flowers, except for my bouquet. This is what it looks like:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\" alt=\"casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;and these will be the bridesmaid ones:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\" alt=\"BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Ceremony&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So as I said before, I needed that terrace for our wedding! which we managed to get, for a surcharge of $1700&amp;nbsp; :huh:. We decided to pay it because it just went with what we had envisioned. We don&#039;t get much for the $1700, it&#039;s still basic decor, so just white garden chairs and you get some perks, but nothing like their $3000 packages, which is fine. I found this picture of the terrace at Azul Beach. I like the one at Azul Fives better but just so you can get an idea&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f3.png\" alt=\"ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are not doing much in terms of decor, just renting two white sheers for the gazebo and placing some pomanders along the asile in alternating chairs that I got from Michael&#039;s. This is what they look like, please forgive the fact that they&#039;re hanging off my cabinets haha, I wanted to see how they looked against white:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\" alt=\"pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;That&#039;s pretty much it for decor for the ceremony, we might add a small (fake) flower arrangement on the table but I&#039;m letting nature take care of the rest :).&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Reception&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/b&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Because I love that terrace so much, we&#039;re also having our reception here. We also upgraded this and we&#039;re paying a surcharge per person added on to the price of the menu.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We decided on a buffet style menu a long time ago, even before we knew when or where we would get married. We just wanted our guests to eat as much as they pleased :). We chose a BBQ style menu which has so many options that I think anyone would be able to find something they like.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In terms of decor, I bit the bullet here, we&#039;re paying for one of the packages for the tables. These are not cheap, but I basically only have to bring my centerpieces. I posted a picture before and here is another one of how the place setting looks:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps5f56eb7d.jpg\" alt=\"ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Then these are the centerpieces I put together:&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\" alt=\"mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The bridesmaid bouquets will double as centerpieces so there is less stuff to bring. The little blue round thing is actually a filled cookie called an alfajor. They&#039;re traditional in Argentina, where I&#039;m from, and my mom has a business here where she makes them. Those will be our favors and they&#039;ll go in the little box. They can be stored quite well for a few weeks so they&#039;ll taste great even when bringing them from home :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Most of this stuff I got at Michael&#039;s, except for the lanterns (Ikea) and the favor boxes, which I got a long time ago from Ebay. They were one of the first things I bought and I paid somewhere around $36 for 100 of them.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Then this is what our sweetheart table will look like. You really have to use your imagination for this one! haha it makes me laugh every time. The middle bouquet will actually be my bouquet.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\" alt=\"mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Now I realize I should have started this thread a long time ago. I just noticed I have a lot of things planned so I have to write these novel-sized entries to catch up and show you guys everything so far haha. Most of this stuff I&#039;ve posted randomly in different threads but it&#039;s nice to have it all in one place.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;That&#039;s it for tonight. I think I managed to put everything I had written in my previous entry that got deleted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next up, my personal favorite, the attire&amp;nbsp; :wub:&amp;nbsp; :D&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886007,"PostDate":1423638223,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>noo, so I had made a suuper long entry and it got deleted <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/>. I'll do my best to replicate it.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ok so now the fun begins!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The wedding band<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>this was literally the first thing I bought. I spent more than I had hoped on it, but then I thought that if I was going to spend my money on something, this should be it. I'll be wearing it for the rest of my life! The band is a matching set with my e-ring, which actually took a lot of work to match. Long story short, it didn't fit well wit my e-ring so I had to send it back a couple of times until it finally got fixed. It was frustrating to say the least but now I can't wait to wear it <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\" alt=\"weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The Flowers<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>If there is one topic that gets me roiled up, is the price of the natural flowers at the Karisma properties. HOLY COW! that's all I have to say haha. To give you an idea, they cost more than what I would pay here in Canada, and they don't allow outside florists. So, I'm boycotting the whole thing and using fake flowers, except for my bouquet. This is what it looks like:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\" alt=\"casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>and these will be the bridesmaid ones:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\" alt=\"BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The Ceremony<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So as I said before, I needed that terrace for our wedding! which we managed to get, for a surcharge of $1700\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/huh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':huh:' \/>. We decided to pay it because it just went with what we had envisioned. We don't get much for the $1700, it's still basic decor, so just white garden chairs and you get some perks, but nothing like their $3000 packages, which is fine. I found this picture of the terrace at Azul Beach. I like the one at Azul Fives better but just so you can get an idea\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f3.png\" alt=\"ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are not doing much in terms of decor, just renting two white sheers for the gazebo and placing some pomanders along the asile in alternating chairs that I got from Michael's. This is what they look like, please forgive the fact that they're hanging off my cabinets haha, I wanted to see how they looked against white:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\" alt=\"pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's pretty much it for decor for the ceremony, we might add a small (fake) flower arrangement on the table but I'm letting nature take care of the rest <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><b><u>The Reception<\/u><\/b><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Because I love that terrace so much, we're also having our reception here. We also upgraded this and we're paying a surcharge per person added on to the price of the menu.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We decided on a buffet style menu a long time ago, even before we knew when or where we would get married. We just wanted our guests to eat as much as they pleased <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. We chose a BBQ style menu which has so many options that I think anyone would be able to find something they like.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In terms of decor, I bit the bullet here, we're paying for one of the packages for the tables. These are not cheap, but I basically only have to bring my centerpieces. I posted a picture before and here is another one of how the place setting looks:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps5f56eb7d.jpg\" alt=\"ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Then these are the centerpieces I put together:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\" alt=\"mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The bridesmaid bouquets will double as centerpieces so there is less stuff to bring. The little blue round thing is actually a filled cookie called an alfajor. They're traditional in Argentina, where I'm from, and my mom has a business here where she makes them. Those will be our favors and they'll go in the little box. They can be stored quite well for a few weeks so they'll taste great even when bringing them from home <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Most of this stuff I got at Michael's, except for the lanterns (Ikea) and the favor boxes, which I got a long time ago from Ebay. They were one of the first things I bought and I paid somewhere around $36 for 100 of them.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Then this is what our sweetheart table will look like. You really have to use your imagination for this one! haha it makes me laugh every time. The middle bouquet will actually be my bouquet.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\" alt=\"mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Now I realize I should have started this thread a long time ago. I just noticed I have a lot of things planned so I have to write these novel-sized entries to catch up and show you guys everything so far haha. Most of this stuff I've posted randomly in different threads but it's nice to have it all in one place.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's it for tonight. I think I managed to put everything I had written in my previous entry that got deleted.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Next up, my personal favorite, the attire\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wub.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':wub:' \/>\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359763104,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1f1e591018d3261cb2ff50f3ce325e35","RawContent":"Awesome and I&#039;ll be honest. Your ceremony site doesn&#039;t need anymore than you&#039;ve planned - trust me. Breathtaking. Don&#039;t kill the scenery with decor is what I say :) what you&#039;ve decided on is gorgeous. \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\nOh and ps - was it spence who\n\nCouldn&#039;t get the band shaped right? Did you send the e-ring with??\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1886025,"PostDate":1423663146,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Awesome and I'll be honest. Your ceremony site doesn't need anymore than you've planned - trust me. Breathtaking. Don't kill the scenery with decor is what I say <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> what you've decided on is gorgeous. <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<br \/>Oh and ps - was it spence who<br>\nCouldn't get the band shaped right? Did you send the e-ring with??<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399428602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.51.153.112","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"894c193012416459ea2161043dc2f99e","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1886007\" timestamp=\"1423638223\"]\nnoo, so I had made a suuper long entry and it got deleted :(. I&#039;ll do my best to replicate it. \n\nOk so now the fun begins! \n\n[b][u]The wedding band[\/u][\/b]\n\nthis was literally the first thing I bought. I spent more than I had hoped on it, but then I thought that if I was going to spend my money on something, this should be it. I&#039;ll be wearing it for the rest of my life! The band is a matching set with my e-ring, which actually took a lot of work to match. Long story short, it didn&#039;t fit well wit my e-ring so I had to send it back a couple of times until it finally got fixed. It was frustrating to say the least but now I can&#039;t wait to wear it :)\n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg[\/img]\n\n[b][u]The Flowers[\/u][\/b]\n\nIf there is one topic that gets me roiled up, is the price of the natural flowers at the Karisma properties. HOLY COW! that&#039;s all I have to say haha. To give you an idea, they cost more than what I would pay here in Canada, and they don&#039;t allow outside florists. So, I&#039;m boycotting the whole thing and using fake flowers, except for my bouquet. This is what it looks like: \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg[\/img]\n\nand these will be the bridesmaid ones: \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg[\/img]\n\n[b][u]The Ceremony[\/u][\/b]\n\nSo as I said before, I needed that terrace for our wedding! which we managed to get, for a surcharge of $1700  :huh:. We decided to pay it because it just went with what we had envisioned. We don&#039;t get much for the $1700, it&#039;s still basic decor, so just white garden chairs and you get some perks, but nothing like their $3000 packages, which is fine. I found this picture of the terrace at Azul Beach. I like the one at Azul Fives better but just so you can get an idea \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f3.png[\/img]\n\nWe are not doing much in terms of decor, just renting two white sheers for the gazebo and placing some pomanders along the asile in alternating chairs that I got from Michael&#039;s. This is what they look like, please forgive the fact that they&#039;re hanging off my cabinets haha, I wanted to see how they looked against white: \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg[\/img]\n\nThat&#039;s pretty much it for decor for the ceremony, we might add a small (fake) flower arrangement on the table but I&#039;m letting nature take care of the rest :). \n\n[b][u]The Reception[\/u][\/b]\n\nBecause I love that terrace so much, we&#039;re also having our reception here. We also upgraded this and we&#039;re paying a surcharge per person added on to the price of the menu. \n\nWe decided on a buffet style menu a long time ago, even before we knew when or where we would get married. We just wanted our guests to eat as much as they pleased :). We chose a BBQ style menu which has so many options that I think anyone would be able to find something they like. \n\nIn terms of decor, I bit the bullet here, we&#039;re paying for one of the packages for the tables. These are not cheap, but I basically only have to bring my centerpieces. I posted a picture before and here is another one of how the place setting looks: \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps5f56eb7d.jpg[\/img]\n\nThen these are the centerpieces I put together: \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg[\/img]\n\nThe bridesmaid bouquets will double as centerpieces so there is less stuff to bring. The little blue round thing is actually a filled cookie called an alfajor. They&#039;re traditional in Argentina, where I&#039;m from, and my mom has a business here where she makes them. Those will be our favors and they&#039;ll go in the little box. They can be stored quite well for a few weeks so they&#039;ll taste great even when bringing them from home :)\n\nMost of this stuff I got at Michael&#039;s, except for the lanterns (Ikea) and the favor boxes, which I got a long time ago from Ebay. They were one of the first things I bought and I paid somewhere around $36 for 100 of them. \n\nThen this is what our sweetheart table will look like. You really have to use your imagination for this one! haha it makes me laugh every time. The middle bouquet will actually be my bouquet. \n\n[img]http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg[\/img]\n\nNow I realize I should have started this thread a long time ago. I just noticed I have a lot of things planned so I have to write these novel-sized entries to catch up and show you guys everything so far haha. Most of this stuff I&#039;ve posted randomly in different threads but it&#039;s nice to have it all in one place. \n\nThat&#039;s it for tonight. I think I managed to put everything I had written in my previous entry that got deleted. \n\nNext up, my personal favorite, the attire  :wub:  :D[\/quote]Love the wedding band with your E-ring, it looks really good :)\n\nI also love that you are incorporating some of your background into the favours. I love that idea so much.\n\nCan&#039;t wait to see more!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1886047,"PostDate":1423668806,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 10 February 2015 - 11:03 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>noo, so I had made a suuper long entry and it got deleted <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/>. I'll do my best to replicate it.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ok so now the fun begins!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The wedding band<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>this was literally the first thing I bought. I spent more than I had hoped on it, but then I thought that if I was going to spend my money on something, this should be it. I'll be wearing it for the rest of my life! The band is a matching set with my e-ring, which actually took a lot of work to match. Long story short, it didn't fit well wit my e-ring so I had to send it back a couple of times until it finally got fixed. It was frustrating to say the least but now I can't wait to wear it <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\" alt=\"weddingring2_zps0992ef31.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The Flowers<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>If there is one topic that gets me roiled up, is the price of the natural flowers at the Karisma properties. HOLY COW! that's all I have to say haha. To give you an idea, they cost more than what I would pay here in Canada, and they don't allow outside florists. So, I'm boycotting the whole thing and using fake flowers, except for my bouquet. This is what it looks like:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\" alt=\"casablancabig_zpsef5e8c36.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>and these will be the bridesmaid ones:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\" alt=\"BMbouquets1_zpsd13c9183.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>The Ceremony<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So as I said before, I needed that terrace for our wedding! which we managed to get, for a surcharge of $1700\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/huh.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':huh:' \/>. We decided to pay it because it just went with what we had envisioned. We don't get much for the $1700, it's still basic decor, so just white garden chairs and you get some perks, but nothing like their $3000 packages, which is fine. I found this picture of the terrace at Azul Beach. I like the one at Azul Fives better but just so you can get an idea\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f3.png\" alt=\"ScreenShot2015-02-10at94836PM_zps548357f\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are not doing much in terms of decor, just renting two white sheers for the gazebo and placing some pomanders along the asile in alternating chairs that I got from Michael's. This is what they look like, please forgive the fact that they're hanging off my cabinets haha, I wanted to see how they looked against white:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\" alt=\"pomanders_zps2aed71ab.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's pretty much it for decor for the ceremony, we might add a small (fake) flower arrangement on the table but I'm letting nature take care of the rest <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><b><u>The Reception<\/u><\/b><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Because I love that terrace so much, we're also having our reception here. We also upgraded this and we're paying a surcharge per person added on to the price of the menu.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We decided on a buffet style menu a long time ago, even before we knew when or where we would get married. We just wanted our guests to eat as much as they pleased <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. We chose a BBQ style menu which has so many options that I think anyone would be able to find something they like.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In terms of decor, I bit the bullet here, we're paying for one of the packages for the tables. These are not cheap, but I basically only have to bring my centerpieces. I posted a picture before and here is another one of how the place setting looks:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps5f56eb7d.jpg\" alt=\"ba078412-9fd7-4387-844b-e1c2865c6af2_zps\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Then these are the centerpieces I put together:\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\" alt=\"mockcenterpieces_zps1ab33086.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The bridesmaid bouquets will double as centerpieces so there is less stuff to bring. The little blue round thing is actually a filled cookie called an alfajor. They're traditional in Argentina, where I'm from, and my mom has a business here where she makes them. Those will be our favors and they'll go in the little box. They can be stored quite well for a few weeks so they'll taste great even when bringing them from home <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Most of this stuff I got at Michael's, except for the lanterns (Ikea) and the favor boxes, which I got a long time ago from Ebay. They were one of the first things I bought and I paid somewhere around $36 for 100 of them.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Then this is what our sweetheart table will look like. You really have to use your imagination for this one! haha it makes me laugh every time. The middle bouquet will actually be my bouquet.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/i1369.photobucket.com\/albums\/ag222\/sblopezb\/mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\" alt=\"mocksweethearttable_zps6660bf78.jpg\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Now I realize I should have started this thread a long time ago. I just noticed I have a lot of things planned so I have to write these novel-sized entries to catch up and show you guys everything so far haha. Most of this stuff I've posted randomly in different threads but it's nice to have it all in one place.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's it for tonight. I think I managed to put everything I had written in my previous entry that got deleted.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Next up, my personal favorite, the attire\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wub.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':wub:' \/>\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Love the wedding band with your E-ring, it looks really good <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I also love that you are incorporating some of your background into the favours. I love that idea so much.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can't wait to see more!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;1\/st\/20151215\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/ec4b\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><br><br><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1419437814,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1428347017","PhotoWidth":169,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.35.43.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7b530cae0f01fd320c0765494c997180","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Your e-ring and wedding band look so great together! Only 6 more months until you get to wear them together :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I love the decor and can&#039;t wait to see your pics with that spectacular background.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886058,"PostDate":1423673424,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Your e-ring and wedding band look so great together! Only 6 more months until you get to wear them together <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>I love the decor and can't wait to see your pics with that spectacular background.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1410098585,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1431039162","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8b2e0e8f955fe538d7319899251f1195","RawContent":"[quote name=\"calgarybride2015\" post=\"1886025\" timestamp=\"1423663146\"]\nAwesome and I&#039;ll be honest. Your ceremony site doesn&#039;t need anymore than you&#039;ve planned - trust me. Breathtaking. Don&#039;t kill the scenery with decor is what I say :) what you&#039;ve decided on is gorgeous.\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\nOh and ps - was it spence who\nCouldn&#039;t get the band shaped right? Did you send the e-ring with??\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk[\/quote]\nThat&#039;s what I was thinking too, it will look great regardless :). I also don&#039;t want to bring so many things plus paying for a huge set-up fee once I get there. \n\nYeah it was Spence. First the wedding band didn&#039;t match because they didn&#039;t tell me to also send my e-ring when it got done, then I send them both back and they wanted to charge me but I told them it wasn&#039;t my fault. Then when I get it back, my e-ring was too big for some reason, even though it fit perfectly fine before. so i had to send them back again and then finally they were perfect :)\n[quote name=\"perianjay\" post=\"1886047\" timestamp=\"1423668806\"]\nLove the wedding band with your E-ring, it looks really good :)\n\nI also love that you are incorporating some of your background into the favours. I love that idea so much.\n\nCan&#039;t wait to see more!![\/quote]\nthanks! yeah, my mom offered to make them to me for free, which is great and saves me on a lot of costs :D \n[quote name=\"Wafflesmom\" post=\"1886058\" timestamp=\"1423673424\"]\nYour e-ring and wedding band look so great together! Only 6 more months until you get to wear them together :)\nI love the decor and can&#039;t wait to see your pics with that spectacular background.[\/quote]thanks! Yay, it&#039;s going to be the longest 6 months ever! hahaha. There&#039;s just a lot of things happening in our lives in these 6 months so it&#039;s super exciting :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1886152,"PostDate":1423752785,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>calgarybride2015, on 11 February 2015 - 05:59 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Awesome and I'll be honest. Your ceremony site doesn't need anymore than you've planned - trust me. Breathtaking. Don't kill the scenery with decor is what I say <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> what you've decided on is gorgeous.<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<br>\nOh and ps - was it spence who<br>\nCouldn't get the band shaped right? Did you send the e-ring with??<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That's what I was thinking too, it will look great regardless <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. I also don't want to bring so many things plus paying for a huge set-up fee once I get there.\u00a0<br><br>\nYeah it was Spence. First the wedding band didn't match because they didn't tell me to also send my e-ring when it got done, then I send them both back and they wanted to charge me but I told them it wasn't my fault. Then when I get it back, my e-ring was too big for some reason, even though it fit perfectly fine before. so i had to send them back again and then finally they were perfect <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>perianjay, on 11 February 2015 - 07:33 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Love the wedding band with your E-ring, it looks really good <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I also love that you are incorporating some of your background into the favours. I love that idea so much.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can't wait to see more!!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>thanks! yeah, my mom offered to make them to me for free, which is great and saves me on a lot of costs <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>Wafflesmom, on 11 February 2015 - 08:50 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Your e-ring and wedding band look so great together! Only 6 more months until you get to wear them together <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>I love the decor and can't wait to see your pics with that spectacular background.\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>thanks! Yay, it's going to be the longest 6 months ever! hahaha. There's just a lot of things happening in our lives in these 6 months so it's super exciting <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359763104,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9fed5a471ebde8056761a98dbc98dd3d","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1886152\" timestamp=\"1423752785\"]\nThat&#039;s what I was thinking too, it will look great regardless :). I also don&#039;t want to bring so many things plus paying for a huge set-up fee once I get there. \n\nYeah it was Spence. First the wedding band didn&#039;t match because they didn&#039;t tell me to also send my e-ring when it got done, then I send them both back and they wanted to charge me but I told them it wasn&#039;t my fault. Then when I get it back, my e-ring was too big for some reason, even though it fit perfectly fine before. so i had to send them back again and then finally they were perfect :)\n\n\nthanks! yeah, my mom offered to make them to me for free, which is great and saves me on a lot of costs :D\n\nthanks! Yay, it&#039;s going to be the longest 6 months ever! hahaha. There&#039;s just a lot of things happening in our lives in these 6 months so it&#039;s super exciting :)[\/quote]I bet it&#039;s flying by quickly though. I feel like time is moving so fast and i&#039;m so consumed by all of this wedding planning. I think my 10 months is going to fly by!!\nI&#039;m excited for you! It&#039;s just sad that all of this planning that we do is for one day that&#039;s going to happen so quickly,","Attachments":[],"Id":1886163,"PostDate":1423759322,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 12 February 2015 - 06:53 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>That's what I was thinking too, it will look great regardless <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. I also don't want to bring so many things plus paying for a huge set-up fee once I get there.\u00a0<br><br>\nYeah it was Spence. First the wedding band didn't match because they didn't tell me to also send my e-ring when it got done, then I send them both back and they wanted to charge me but I told them it wasn't my fault. Then when I get it back, my e-ring was too big for some reason, even though it fit perfectly fine before. so i had to send them back again and then finally they were perfect <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>thanks! yeah, my mom offered to make them to me for free, which is great and saves me on a lot of costs <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>thanks! Yay, it's going to be the longest 6 months ever! hahaha. There's just a lot of things happening in our lives in these 6 months so it's super exciting <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>I bet it's flying by quickly though. I feel like time is moving so fast and i'm so consumed by all of this wedding planning. I think my 10 months is going to fly by!!<\/p>\n<p>I'm excited for you! It's just sad that all of this planning that we do is for one day that's going to happen so quickly,<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;1\/st\/20151215\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/ec4b\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><br><br><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1419437814,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1428347017","PhotoWidth":169,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"208.98.196.2","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ea1f05ece9b61b6df9c87157da737d85","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"perianjay\"] A good way of looking at it is that at least we get to spend a whole week with our loved ones enjoying ourselves, vs. only one day when we do it at home. I always get kind of depressed the day after a party, but this way we keep the party going for a bit longer haha. There&#039;s actually 4 birthdays and 3 anniversaries (4 with ours now actually) in the days we&#039;ll be in Mexico. We will all have reason to celebrate :D, and to keep celebrating ahaha. My friends are already saying it&#039;s going to be insane :P.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I think the day of the wedding will give me that feeling that you got when you&#039;re a kid and you&#039;re about to open your christmas gift. All that excitement and anticipation that has been building up for days (in this case months for this wedding) reaches its maximum level when you&#039;re right in front of the gift, ready to open it. You know that the amazing feeling will be over the second you open it, and you&#039;re torn between feeling that and actually knowing what the gift has inside. That was always my favorite moment of getting a gift :), the second before I opened it. I don&#039;t know if anyone else ever gets that but that&#039;s how I feel about this wedding.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It is flying by rather quickly! And now that I put all the planning into high gear especially. I remember I was a year out when i started really planning and I felt like time would never pass but it has gone by super quickly :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886165,"PostDate":1423760109,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> A good way of looking at it is that at least we get to spend a whole week with our loved ones enjoying ourselves, vs. only one day when we do it at home. I always get kind of depressed the day after a party, but this way we keep the party going for a bit longer haha. There's actually 4 birthdays and 3 anniversaries (4 with ours now actually) in the days we'll be in Mexico. We will all have reason to celebrate <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/>, and to keep celebrating ahaha. My friends are already saying it's going to be insane <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/>.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think the day of the wedding will give me that feeling that you got when you're a kid and you're about to open your christmas gift. All that excitement and anticipation that has been building up for days (in this case months for this wedding) reaches its maximum level when you're right in front of the gift, ready to open it. You know that the amazing feeling will be over the second you open it, and you're torn between feeling that and actually knowing what the gift has inside. That was always my favorite moment of getting a gift <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>, the second before I opened it. I don't know if anyone else ever gets that but that's how I feel about this wedding.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It is flying by rather quickly! And now that I put all the planning into high gear especially. I remember I was a year out when i started really planning and I felt like time would never pass but it has gone by super quickly <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359763104,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4daf28b2bd5810a46fc36f8a8f0c5b90","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1886165\" timestamp=\"1423760109\"]\n@[member=\"perianjay\"] A good way of looking at it is that at least we get to spend a whole week with our loved ones enjoying ourselves, vs. only one day when we do it at home. I always get kind of depressed the day after a party, but this way we keep the party going for a bit longer haha. There&#039;s actually 4 birthdays and 3 anniversaries (4 with ours now actually) in the days we&#039;ll be in Mexico. We will all have reason to celebrate :D, and to keep celebrating ahaha. My friends are already saying it&#039;s going to be insane :P.\n\nI think the day of the wedding will give me that feeling that you got when you&#039;re a kid and you&#039;re about to open your christmas gift. All that excitement and anticipation that has been building up for days (in this case months for this wedding) reaches its maximum level when you&#039;re right in front of the gift, ready to open it. You know that the amazing feeling will be over the second you open it, and you&#039;re torn between feeling that and actually knowing what the gift has inside. That was always my favorite moment of getting a gift :), the second before I opened it. I don&#039;t know if anyone else ever gets that but that&#039;s how I feel about this wedding. \n\nIt is flying by rather quickly! And now that I put all the planning into high gear especially. I remember I was a year out when i started really planning and I felt like time would never pass but it has gone by super quickly :)[\/quote]That is the perfect way to describe it!! I am so excited for that moment as well. :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1886181,"PostDate":1423765984,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 12 February 2015 - 08:55 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> A good way of looking at it is that at least we get to spend a whole week with our loved ones enjoying ourselves, vs. only one day when we do it at home. I always get kind of depressed the day after a party, but this way we keep the party going for a bit longer haha. There's actually 4 birthdays and 3 anniversaries (4 with ours now actually) in the days we'll be in Mexico. We will all have reason to celebrate <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/biggrin.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':D' \/>, and to keep celebrating ahaha. My friends are already saying it's going to be insane <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/>.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think the day of the wedding will give me that feeling that you got when you're a kid and you're about to open your christmas gift. All that excitement and anticipation that has been building up for days (in this case months for this wedding) reaches its maximum level when you're right in front of the gift, ready to open it. You know that the amazing feeling will be over the second you open it, and you're torn between feeling that and actually knowing what the gift has inside. That was always my favorite moment of getting a gift <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>, the second before I opened it. I don't know if anyone else ever gets that but that's how I feel about this wedding.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It is flying by rather quickly! And now that I put all the planning into high gear especially. I remember I was a year out when i started really planning and I felt like time would never pass but it has gone by super quickly <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>That is the perfect way to describe it!! I am so excited for that moment as well. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;1\/st\/20151215\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/ec4b\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><br><br><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1419437814,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1428347017","PhotoWidth":169,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cbeaea61eb849165ef2e2bd3c8fc325d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;But don&#039;t wish the time away --- as I sit here 3 weeks after the wedding a part of me wishes I was still waiting!!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;That sucks about your ring!!! &amp;nbsp;I want to get my solderer together but I think I want a band for the other side which I can&#039;t afford (or don&#039;t want too) right now and not sure I want to get it soldered twice. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;maybe I can get a nice eternity diamond band for my other hand instead hehehe.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886247,"PostDate":1423795405,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>But don't wish the time away --- as I sit here 3 weeks after the wedding a part of me wishes I was still waiting!!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That sucks about your ring!!! \u00a0I want to get my solderer together but I think I want a band for the other side which I can't afford (or don't want too) right now and not sure I want to get it soldered twice. \u00a0 \u00a0maybe I can get a nice eternity diamond band for my other hand instead hehehe.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399428602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78768,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1423800551,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"da83c72d9c7cb5491aa6d4e2a4808b77","RawContent":"[quote name=\"calgarybride2015\" post=\"1886247\" timestamp=\"1423795405\"]\nBut don&#039;t wish the time away --- as I sit here 3 weeks after the wedding a part of me wishes I was still waiting!!!!\n\nThat sucks about your ring!!!  I want to get my solderer together but I think I want a band for the other side which I can&#039;t afford (or don&#039;t want too) right now and not sure I want to get it soldered twice.    maybe I can get a nice eternity diamond band for my other hand instead hehehe.[\/quote]that would be nice. I find they never look \"picture perfect\" unless you&#039;re trying to keep them perfectly together. One of my friends, her wedding band is double and the e-ring goes in the middle. The wedding band has these little stoppers at the bottom so when you put the e-ring in the middle it doesn&#039;t move so much, it looks like it&#039;s all one ring. Basically it can only move from side to side. It&#039;s very hard to explain haha but i wish mine had something like that :P\n\nPS: i can&#039;t believe it&#039;s been 3 weeks already!","Attachments":[],"Id":1886263,"PostDate":1423800509,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>calgarybride2015, on 12 February 2015 - 06:43 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>But don't wish the time away --- as I sit here 3 weeks after the wedding a part of me wishes I was still waiting!!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>That sucks about your ring!!! \u00a0I want to get my solderer together but I think I want a band for the other side which I can't afford (or don't want too) right now and not sure I want to get it soldered twice. \u00a0 \u00a0maybe I can get a nice eternity diamond band for my other hand instead hehehe.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>that would be nice. I find they never look \"picture perfect\" unless you're trying to keep them perfectly together. One of my friends, her wedding band is double and the e-ring goes in the middle. The wedding band has these little stoppers at the bottom so when you put the e-ring in the middle it doesn't move so much, it looks like it's all one ring. Basically it can only move from side to side. It's very hard to explain haha but i wish mine had something like that <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>PS: i can't believe it's been 3 weeks already!\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359763104,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1427386564","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":153,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":426,"TotalPages":43,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":420},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
